1	//! The content plane: chunk framing, DAG assembly, the pin-provider layer,
2	//! verified reads, and version retention (blueprint/engine.md "Content plane").
3	//!
4	//! The engine frames content into fixed-size chunks and seals each with core's
5	//! content-seal primitive under a fresh per-version content key, assembles a DAG
6	//! addressed by the version's `contentCid`, and reads blocks back through the
7	//! trustless gateway with a fail-closed CID verify on every response. All crypto
8	//! and the content-address codec are core's ([`cipherbox_core::content`], #691);
9	//! this plane composes them and owns the framing/DAG shape and the placement,
10	//! quota, and retention judgment (#630).
11	//!
12	//! - [`chunk`] — fixed-size framing + per-version key + core seal + leaf CID.
13	//! - [`dag`] — the version root addressed by its `contentCid`, chunk-aligned.
14	//! - [`provider`] — the pin-provider layer and BYO reachability probe.
15	//! - [`read`] — verified reads (accelerator + public fallback), fail-closed.
16	//! - [`retention`] — pre-flight quota and the explicit prune op.
17	//! - [`profile`] — the open-edge chunk-size constant.
